  "title": "Forbidden City (Imperial Palace), Beijing",
  "summary": "The Forbidden City in Beijing was the Ming and Qing imperial palace from 1420 to 1911, built under the Yongle Emperor between 1406 and 1420. Its largest building, the Hall of Supreme Harmony, stands on a three-tier marble terrace on the central axis. It is a UNESCO World Heritage site.",
